content.thinking:
Interesting! The Fresha test at line 75-80 says: "short-circuits with feature_gated=true when fresha_sync flag is off. No signature provided — should still 200 because we exit before signature check."

This means the feature gate check in FreshaCatalogWebhookController currently happens BEFORE signature validation:
```php
if (! (bool) config('sidest.features.fresha_sync', false)) {
    Log::info('Fresha webhook suppressed — fresha_sync feature flag is off');
    return $this->success(['received' => true, 'feature_gated' => true]);


}
```

If I move signature validation to middleware, the middleware runs BEFORE the controller — meaning the feature gate check would run AFTER signature validation. This would break the test: with no signature and feature flag off, the current behavior is 200 (feature_gated), but with middleware it would be 401 (invalid signature).

Square has the same pattern with its feature flag check, so I need to verify whether its test expects the same behavior.

